// @reject: `$+` on a tuple as a bare statement would have to modify it,
// @reject: and a tuple does not change. The functional form
// @reject: `otro = t$+ 3` is the one that exists — it derives a new
// @reject: tuple, as (1,2) + (3,) does in Python.
// @reject: Built 2026-08-18 with decision 12: a bare `$` edit statement
// @reject: modifies its receiver, and the receiver check refuses a
// @reject: positional tuple whatever the operator — immutability is a
// @reject: property of the value, not an exception inside each `$`.
t = (1, 2)
t$+ 3
